                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Game isn't that bad at all. Gameplay is relaxing, price isn't high. If someone want to play such simple and inflexible platformer then game is fine to play.\n\nBut after playing about 1/3 or 1/2 of game, I have few problems, that make me angry at playing. Game is unfair, that's why:\n- in few places you just can't dodge damage (because gateway height - enemy height is lower than character height)\n- enemies can hurt you at jumping on them, in some cases when enemy turn around and you will touch him (even from above) you just will get damage from it, I think enemies change their hitbox, thats why, but still, you just can't know when you will get damage\n- moving platforms when they move down makes you non stop falling down, and you can't jump from such platform, it's bizarre if you need to wait until platform will go higher possible height and then platform just block your jump, so you will fall down into water\n\nApart from these big problems, the game also has some problems with accessibility:\n- moving around menu force you to using mouse instead of keyboard, it's annoying, and stupid (smell like mobile games)\n- game asks us if we want to pass trough money blocking place (we need to have at least X money to move ahead), it's okay, but asking is just useless, we can't spend money on other things, we can't collect infinite amount of money, so why game enforce me to use mouse in keyboard/gamepad game to \"accept\" those things?\n- can't adjust sound volume (there are just toggle, like in most mobile games)\n\nSummarizing: game is fine if you want to play some platformer thats looks like free mobile game, but I can't recommend you to buy it if game is just unfair or have such problems with accessibility.",
